---
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Site
  title="About KajLights"
  description="Why learn electronics, computing and communications through microcontrollers? Understand how things work so you can imagine, ask for and make more."
>
  <section class="wrap page-intro narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">PLAY · INVESTIGATE · MAKE</p>
    <h1>
      Understand more.
      <br />
      Imagine more.
    </h1>
    <p class="intro">
      KajLights is a practical way into electronics, computing and networking
      through microcontrollers, light and sound.
    </p>
    <p>
      A small board can connect an idea to something you can see, hear or
      measure. Making it work brings together a circuit, a program and signals
      between components or devices. Our aim is to help people understand those
      relationships and use them to make things of their own.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap section narrow prose">
    <h2>Learn through the whole system</h2>
    <p>
      Coding is part of the picture. So are power and current, the role of a
      processor, how information is represented, and the rules that let devices
      communicate. A light pattern makes these ideas tangible: you can enjoy it,
      change it, investigate it and explain it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Play, investigation and making are equally valid ways in. You can start
      with the browser preview, follow a guided lesson, trace a circuit or work
      towards a project you have imagined. The{" "}
      <a href={`${base}learn/`}>learning path</a> connects electronics,
      computing and communications without requiring a single order or a
      particular programming language.
    </p>
    <h2 id="why-understanding">
      Why understanding matters in an AI-ready world
    </h2>
    <p>
      When you can ask an AI assistant to help build something, knowing what is
      possible becomes especially useful. Understanding sensors, computation and
      communications gives you ideas to combine, constraints to describe and
      questions to ask. It also helps you test whether the result does what you
      intended.
    </p>
    <blockquote class="learning-prompt">
      If you can’t imagine it, you can’t ask for it to be built.
    </blockquote>
    <p>
      The ambition is to give imagination more material to work with. Learn
      enough to notice a possibility, describe it clearly, try a small version
      and judge the evidence. Those habits matter whether you make something by
      hand, work with another person or use AI. No AI service or account is
      required to take part in KajLights.
    </p>
    <h2>A shared aim with Found in Space</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="https://foundin.space/about/">Found in Space</a> approaches the
      same ambition through scientific data and models: explore an experience,
      question the evidence behind it and build with its materials. KajLights
      approaches it through circuits, microcontrollers and connected systems.
      Both aim to help people understand what they can ask, imagine what they
      could make and assess what an answer or a working example really shows.
    </p>
    <h2>What is available now?</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>LightVM</strong> runs lighting programs on supported boards and in
      the browser preview. Its editor offers Python, JavaScript, visual blocks
      and twelve beginner lessons. This site adds hardware guidance, an early
      learning path and tools for managing devices and available firmware.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>kaj-fi</strong> explores sound analysis and sharing derived audio
      features between devices while keeping raw sound on the analyser. Its
      public firmware distribution is not yet enabled. Networking and audio
      capabilities depend on the board and firmware features in use.
    </p>
    <h2>Early testing, with room to improve</h2>
    <p>
      These are experimental projects. Expect bugs, missing features and gaps in
      the instructions. Changes can require wiping and setting up a board again.
      A supported development board is not a promise of a tested public
      installer; check the <a href={`${base}releases/`}>release catalogue</a>{" "}
      before planning hardware setup.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our learning aims and investigation prompts are ambitions to test and
      improve, not claims of evaluated learning outcomes. Teachers and learners
      can help by sharing where an explanation or activity needs more work.
    </p>
    <h2>Your browser, your devices</h2>
    <p>
      Device connections run directly in your browser. No KajLights account or
      cloud device database is required. Remembered labels stay in this browser;
      nicknames you explicitly save are written to the device. Firmware assets
      come from the website’s verified release mirror.
    </p>
    <h2>Help make the workshop</h2>
    <p>
      Bring a question, a correction, a project or an explanation that helped
      something click.{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/KajLights/KajLights.github.io/issues">
        Share feedback on the website and guides
      </a>
      , or{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/KajLights">
        explore the implementation projects
      </a>
      . Useful contributions include clearer pictures and experiments as well as
      code.
    </p>
  </section>
</Site>
